    "label": "Appendix 3 - D1 Scenario",
    "description": "Comprehensive foot care intervention to prevent lower extremity amputations in people with diabetes.\nThis scenario exposes the parameters for neuropathy screening and foot care programs that work by early detection and management of diabetic neuropathy complications.\nThe intervention reduces progression from diabetes to lower extremity amputation by providing educational programs, access to appropriate footwear, and multidisciplinary clinic care.\nNeuropathy screening identifies at-risk individuals with diabetic nerve damage who require enhanced foot care, with a target population in need of 66% of diabetic patients.\nThe intervention includes systematic foot examinations, patient education on foot care practices, provision of therapeutic footwear, and coordinated care through specialized clinics.\nThis intervention is particularly effective in preventing costly and debilitating amputations while improving quality of life for people with diabetes.\nNote: This intervention should be implemented alongside other diabetes care interventions for comprehensive management of diabetes complications.\n",
